### Manual requests for the Redirector API (VS Code REST Client / Visual Studio .http support).
###
### 1. Start the stack:   docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yml up -d
### 2. Create a link with the Shortener API (see UrlShortener.Shortener.Api.http) and copy its short code.
### 3. Run the API:       dotnet run --project src/UrlShortener.Redirector.Api --launch-profile http
###
### The editor follows redirects by default; to see the 302 itself, turn that off (REST Client setting
### "rest-client.followRedirect") or use: curl -i http://localhost:5136/<code>

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5136
@shortCode = PASTE-A-SHORT-CODE

### Follow a short link: 302 with Location and Cache-Control
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{shortCode}}

### Unknown code: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist

### Not a possible short code: 404 (answered without any lookup)
GET {{baseUrl}}/favicon.ico

### An expired link answers 410 Gone: create one with expires_at a few seconds ahead, wait, then request it
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{shortCode}}
